# /etc/lsevin-alerter/telegram.env on server B (mode 600). Create the bot with @BotFather, send it any message, then
# open https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates to read "chat":{"id":...}. A group chat id is negative.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# Chat(s) (channel or private) for everything that is NOT critical (warnings, info, daily summary, startup), comma separated.
# Production: the muted channel "Lsevin monitoring", checked whenever there is time.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Chat(s) for CRITICAL messages only (new / still open / resolved criticals, MONITORING BROKEN); a critical alert is only announced after it has
# lasted critical_min_for_seconds (rules.json, 600). Production: the channel "lsevin critical" with notifications on. Channel ids look like
# -100xxxxxxxxxx and the bot must be an administrator of the channel. If this line is empty/missing, every message goes to every chat in
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID (old behaviour).
TELEGRAM_CRITICAL_CHAT_ID=
